WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.601
Phones, printers, speakers, consoles,
TVs and watches all join the network.

2
00:00:09.821 --> 00:00:13.351
Joined together, two devices
do what neither can alone.

3
00:00:13.851 --> 00:00:18.216
A network is not only computers.
Lots of devices can join one.

4
00:00:18.436 --> 00:00:23.823
A laptop browses the web. A tablet
plays videos, games and messages.

5
00:00:24.043 --> 00:00:28.734
A phone joins at home. A printer
prints for every device in the house.

6
00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:33.830
A smart speaker fetches music. A
games console plays with a friend.

7
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.205
A smart TV streams a film. A smart
watch shows messages on your wrist.

8
00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:43.372
A wooden chair cannot join,
because it has no computer inside.

9
00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:46.936
The others all join through the
router, and reach the internet.

10
00:00:47.436 --> 00:00:50.733
A phone takes a photo, but
a phone cannot print it.

11
00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:54.250
A printer prints, but a
printer cannot take a photo.

12
00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.953
Join them both to the network.
Now the photo can travel.

13
00:00:58.173 --> 00:01:02.399
The phone sends it. The printer
prints it. Neither could do both.

14
00:01:02.619 --> 00:01:08.563
A phone holds a song, and a speaker
plays it loud. Two devices, one job.

15
00:01:09.063 --> 00:01:12.361
A wired network joins
its devices with cables.

16
00:01:12.581 --> 00:01:15.971
An office has a cable from
every computer to the wall.

17
00:01:16.191 --> 00:01:19.488
A school computer room has
cables under the desks.

18
00:01:19.708 --> 00:01:23.470
A wireless network joins them
through the air, with wi-fi.

19
00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:28.937
Tablets at home and phones on a train
are wireless. Many places have both.

20
00:01:29.437 --> 00:01:32.549
Your device tells you
whether the network is there.

21
00:01:32.769 --> 00:01:36.902
Bars on the phone mean it is
available. So does a green light.

22
00:01:37.122 --> 00:01:41.116
No bars, aeroplane mode or a
dark router mean it is not.

23
00:01:41.336 --> 00:01:45.376
A page that spins and never
loads usually means no network.

24
00:01:45.596 --> 00:01:50.054
Then the things that need other
devices stop, and the rest carry on.

25
00:01:50.554 --> 00:01:54.037
Devices on a network share
information with each other.

26
00:01:54.257 --> 00:01:57.647
What you send is seen by
every device it goes to.

27
00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:03.208
A message to the class group goes to
the whole class. Think before you send.

28
00:02:03.428 --> 00:02:07.004
Something posted for anyone to
see can be seen by strangers.

29
00:02:07.504 --> 00:02:13.541
Your full name, your address, your
school: that is personal information.

30
00:02:13.761 --> 00:02:17.244
Share it on a network, and
you cannot take it back.

31
00:02:17.464 --> 00:02:21.086
A password is for you and a
grown-up only. Keep it private.

32
00:02:21.306 --> 00:02:25.857
Some files are malware, made to do
harm. Never open one from a stranger.

33
00:02:26.357 --> 00:02:30.537
Lots of devices join a network,
and through it, the internet.

34
00:02:30.757 --> 00:02:36.191
Two together do what neither can alone.
Cables are wired, wi-fi is wireless.

35
00:02:36.411 --> 00:02:40.869
Bars and lights say it is there.
Think who will see what you share.
